  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 137 AM CDT Wed Jun 3 2026\n\nModest rain chances continue into the extended as an upper shear \naxis remains stationary from western Oklahoma to southeastern New \nMexico and into Mexico. The rain and cloud cover will keep \ntemperatures below normal through the end of the week as highs \nremain in the 80s. \n\nLow pressure develops on the southern end of this axis over \nMexico and moves northeast into Texas on Saturday, then leaving \nthe region on Sunday. Rain chances come to an end with the exit of\nthe low as a ridge builds in and provides increasing stability. \nHighs rise back up to near normal next week as highs get back into\nthe 90s.\n\nHennig",
